                        <section id="work">
                            <h2 class="mb-3 mt-5 mb-3">👨‍💻 Work</h2>
                        </section>
                        <p>I am currently the Innovation lead at Woodside energy. I started my career there working as a full stack robotics engineer at <a href="https://www.woodside.com/media-centre/news-stories/story/introducing-spector-a-woodside-robotics-first"
                            target="_blank">Woodside Energy</a>, working on
                            deployment of robotic systems across our facilities for remote inspections. I am also a technical specialist in the Australian Defence Force. Its awesome, reach out if you are interested.</p>

                        <section id="education">
                            <h2 class="mb-3 mt-5 mb-3">👨‍🎓 Education</h2>
                        </section>
                        <p>As an undergraduate I studied Physics, Applied Mathematics and Mechanical Engineering. I then did my PhD in submarine vibration for the sonar systems team
                            at Defence Science and Technology for the Australian Defence Force. Never start work before you
                            finish your PhD, take it from me (I have a <a href="/blog/phd/" target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer">blog</a> on it). I am now actively pushing my learning and development in the field of artificial intelligence and robotics. </p>

                        <section id="speaking">
                            <h2 class="mb-3 mt-5 mb-3">🎤 Public Speaking</h2>
                        </section>
                        <p>I am a semi-retired public speaking competitor, but I still love it (and always willing to come out of retirement). I was lucky to be the
                            president of a <a href="https://www.rostrum.com.au/" target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer">Rostrum</a> public speaking club in Perth, which pushed me to win an <a href="/blog/ypwl/" target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer">international competition</a>.
                            </p>

                        <section id="speaking">
                            <h2 class="mb-3 mt-5 mb-3">🧗‍ Hobbies</h2>
                        </section>

                        <ul>
                            <li> <b>Rock climbing</b> - My one true obsession. What I love about rock climbing is that it combined physical (strength, power, flexibility, mobility), mental (problem solving, overcoming fear, performance under stress) and technical (climbing skill, roping methods). It also a hobby that I can travel and explore the world with, getting out in nature. What I also love is that rock climbing is not a zero sum sport, my success does not come at someone else’s loss, and everyone can celebrate each others endeavours. Outdoor exploration to date:
                                <ul>
                                <li> <b>Australia</b> - Kalbarri, Margaret River, Albany, Mount Arapiles, Blue Mountains, Kangaroo Point, Mount Tinbeerwah and Mount Coolum.
                                </li>
                                <li> <b>International</b> - Tonsai Thailand, Boulder Colorado, Dolomites Italy, Kalymnos Greece.
                                </ul>
                                </li>
                            </li>

                            <li> <b>Basketball</b> - Some might say that being white, software development and
                                basketball do not go hand in hand, and they would be right. I am not the best but I love
                                it and I religiously watch the NBA.
                            </li>

                            <li> <b>Magic</b> - This is why I am not good at basketball. They just do not overlap. Card
                                tricks are my thing, I own approximately 40 decks of playing cards. I quite enjoy Clarke's 3rd law - "Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic", which means a magician is simply a purveyor or advanced technology.
                            </li>

                            <li> <b>Stand Up</b> - I have done some amateur comedy (very amateur) which is by far the most
                                terrifying thing I've done.
                            </li>

                        </ul>


                        <section id="travel">
                            <h2 class="mb-3 mt-5 mb-3">🌏 Travel</h2>
                        </section>
                        <p>Here are the countries I have been to.</p>

                        <div id="globe-container" style="width: 100%; max-width: 500px; margin: 0 auto; position: relative; aspect-ratio: 1/1;">
                            <div id="globe-tooltip" style="position: absolute; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0; z-index: 20;
                                padding: 6px 14px; font-size: 11px; font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
                                letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase;
                                border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); background: rgba(10,10,15,0.85);
                                backdrop-filter: blur(8px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
                                color: #e0e0e0; transition: opacity 150ms ease; white-space: nowrap;
                                transform: translate(-50%, -130%);"></div>
                        </div>

                        <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js"></script>
                        <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/topojson-client@3"></script>
                        <script>
                        (async function() {
                            const GLOBE_RADIUS = 90;
                            const DOT_COUNT = 70000;
                            const MARKER_SIZE = 2.0;
                            const AUTO_ROTATE_SPEED = 0.09;
                            const LAND_COLOR = 0x00ff88;
                            const VISITED_COLOR = 0xff00ff;

                            /* ISO 3166-1 numeric codes for visited countries */
                            const VISITED_IDS = new Set([
                                '036','040','124','156','250','276','300','360',
                                '380','392','458','528','554','620','710','756',
                                '826','840','704','136'
                            ]);

                            const markers = [
                                { lng: 133.7, lat: -25.3, name: "Australia" },
                                { lng: 14.6,  lat: 47.5,  name: "Austria" },
                                { lng:-106.3, lat: 56.1,  name: "Canada" },
                                { lng: 104.2, lat: 35.9,  name: "China" },
                                { lng: 2.2,   lat: 46.6,  name: "France" },
                                { lng: 10.5,  lat: 51.2,  name: "Germany" },
                                { lng: 21.8,  lat: 39.1,  name: "Greece" },
                                { lng: 113.9, lat: -0.8,  name: "Indonesia" },
                                { lng: 12.6,  lat: 41.9,  name: "Italy" },
                                { lng: 138.3, lat: 36.2,  name: "Japan" },
                                { lng: 101.7, lat: 4.2,   name: "Malaysia" },
                                { lng: 5.3,   lat: 52.1,  name: "Netherlands" },
                                { lng: 174.9, lat:-40.9,  name: "New Zealand" },
                                { lng: -8.2,  lat: 39.4,  name: "Portugal" },
                                { lng: 24.7,  lat:-28.5,  name: "South Africa" },
                                { lng: 8.2,   lat: 46.8,  name: "Switzerland" },
                                { lng: -3.4,  lat: 55.4,  name: "United Kingdom" },
                                { lng:-95.7,  lat: 37.1,  name: "United States" },
                                { lng: 108.3, lat: 14.1,  name: "Vietnam" },
                                { lng:-81.3,  lat: 19.3,  name: "Cayman Islands" },
                            ];

                            /* ── Load geographic data with visited country classification ── */
                            async function loadLandMask() {
                                const resp = await fetch('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/world-atlas@2/countries-50m.json');
                                const topoData = await resp.json();
                                const countries = topojson.feature(topoData, topoData.objects.countries);
                                const mapW = 4096, mapH = 2048;
                                const offCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
                                offCanvas.width = mapW; offCanvas.height = mapH;
                                const ctx = offCanvas.getContext('2d');
                                ctx.fillStyle = '#000';
                                ctx.fillRect(0, 0, mapW, mapH);
                                function projectCoord(lon, lat) {
                                    return [((lon + 180) / 360) * mapW, ((90 - lat) / 180) * mapH];
                                }
                                function drawPolygon(coords) {
                                    ctx.beginPath();
                                    for (let i = 0; i < coords.length; i++) {
                                        const [x, y] = projectCoord(coords[i][0], coords[i][1]);
                                        i === 0 ? ctx.moveTo(x, y) : ctx.lineTo(x, y);
                                    }
                                    ctx.closePath();
                                    ctx.fill();
                                }
                                function processGeometry(geom) {
                                    if (geom.type === 'Polygon') geom.coordinates.forEach(ring => drawPolygon(ring));
                                    else if (geom.type === 'MultiPolygon') geom.coordinates.forEach(poly => poly.forEach(ring => drawPolygon(ring)));
                                    else if (geom.type === 'GeometryCollection') geom.geometries.forEach(g => processGeometry(g));
                                }
                                /* Draw unvisited countries in green channel */
                                countries.features.forEach(f => {
                                    if (!VISITED_IDS.has(f.id)) {
                                        ctx.fillStyle = '#00ff00';
                                        processGeometry(f.geometry);
                                    }
                                });
                                /* Draw visited countries in red channel (on top) */
                                countries.features.forEach(f => {
                                    if (VISITED_IDS.has(f.id)) {
                                        ctx.fillStyle = '#ff0000';
                                        processGeometry(f.geometry);
                                    }
                                });
                                return { imageData: ctx.getImageData(0, 0, mapW, mapH), mapW, mapH };
                            }

                            /* Returns: 0 = water, 1 = unvisited land, 2 = visited land */
                            function classifyPoint(lat, lon, imageData, mapW, mapH) {
                                const cx = Math.max(0, Math.min(mapW - 1, Math.floor(((lon + 180) / 360) * mapW)));
                                const cy = Math.max(0, Math.min(mapH - 1, Math.floor(((90 - lat) / 180) * mapH)));
                                const idx = (cy * mapW + cx) * 4;
                                if (imageData.data[idx] > 128) return 2;     /* red = visited */
                                if (imageData.data[idx + 1] > 128) return 1; /* green = unvisited land */
                                return 0;                                     /* water */
                            }

                            /* ── Build the scene ── */
                            const { imageData, mapW, mapH } = await loadLandMask();

                            const container = document.getElementById('globe-container');
                            const tooltip = document.getElementById('globe-tooltip');

                            const BG = 0x050507;

                            const scene = new THREE.Scene();

                            const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(45, 1, 1, 1000);
                            camera.position.set(0, 20, 310);

                            scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.6));
                            const keyLight = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1.0);
                            keyLight.position.set(80, 50, 80);
                            scene.add(keyLight);
                            const rimLight = new THREE.SpotLight(LAND_COLOR, 2.5);
                            rimLight.position.set(-100, 50, -50);
                            rimLight.lookAt(0, 0, 0);
                            scene.add(rimLight);

                            const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: false, alpha: true });
                            renderer.setClearColor(0x000000, 0);
                            renderer.setSize(container.clientWidth, container.clientHeight || container.clientWidth);
                            renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));
                            container.insertBefore(renderer.domElement, container.firstChild);
                            renderer.domElement.style.display = 'block';
                            renderer.domElement.style.width = '100%';
                            renderer.domElement.style.height = '100%';
                            renderer.domElement.style.cursor = 'grab';

                            const globeGroup = new THREE.Group();
                            scene.add(globeGroup);

                            /* ── Occlusion sphere ── */
                            const occlusionMat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: BG });
                            globeGroup.add(new THREE.Mesh(
                                new THREE.SphereGeometry(GLOBE_RADIUS - 0.5, 64, 64), occlusionMat
                            ));

                            /* ── Atmosphere glow ── */
                            const glowMat = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
                                uniforms: { uTime: { value: 0 }, uIntensity: { value: 1.0 } },
                                vertexShader: `
                                    varying vec3 vNormal; varying vec3 vWorldPos;
                                    void main() {
                                        vNormal = normalize(normalMatrix * normal);
                                        vWorldPos = (modelMatrix * vec4(position,1.0)).xyz;
                                        gl_Position = projectionMatrix * modelViewMatrix * vec4(position,1.0);
                                    }`,
                                fragmentShader: `
                                    uniform float uTime; uniform float uIntensity;
                                    varying vec3 vNormal; varying vec3 vWorldPos;
                                    void main() {
                                        float intensity = pow(0.55 - dot(vNormal, vec3(0,0,1.0)), 3.5);
                                        vec3 mint = vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.533);
                                        vec3 blue = vec3(0.0, 0.831, 1.0);
                                        float blend = 0.5 + 0.5 * sin(atan(vWorldPos.y, vWorldPos.x) * 2.0 + uTime * 0.3);
                                        vec3 col = mix(mint, blue, blend * 0.3);
                                        gl_FragColor = vec4(col * intensity * 0.45 * uIntensity, intensity * 0.6 * uIntensity);
                                    }`,
                                side: THREE.BackSide, blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending, transparent: true, depthWrite: false
                            });
                            scene.add(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(GLOBE_RADIUS * 1.18, 64, 64), glowMat));

                            /* ── Dot matrix ── */
                            const dotMaterial = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
                                uniforms: {
                                    uTime: { value: 0 },
                                    uAlphaBoost: { value: 1.0 },
                                    uVisitedColor: { value: new THREE.Color(1.0, 0.0, 1.0) },
                                    uLandColor: { value: new THREE.Color(0.0, 1.0, 0.533) },
                                    uWaterColor: { value: new THREE.Color(0.071, 0.071, 0.133) },
                                },
                                vertexShader: `
                                    attribute float aLandType; attribute float aRandom; uniform float uTime;
                                    varying float vLandType; varying float vAlpha;
                                    void main() {
                                        vLandType = aLandType;
                                        float twinkle = sin(uTime*1.5 + aRandom*62.831)*0.15+0.85;
                                        float waterPulse = sin(uTime*0.5 + aRandom*31.415)*0.1+0.9;
                                        float visitedPulse = sin(uTime*2.0 + aRandom*62.831)*0.1+0.9;
                                        float scale;
                                        if (aLandType > 1.5) { vAlpha = visitedPulse; scale = 1.8; }
                                        else if (aLandType > 0.5) { vAlpha = twinkle; scale = 1.6; }
                                        else { vAlpha = waterPulse * 0.45; scale = 0.6; }
                                        vec4 mvPos = modelViewMatrix * vec4(position,1.0);
                                        gl_PointSize = scale * (300.0 / -mvPos.z);
                                        gl_Position = projectionMatrix * mvPos;
                                    }`,
                                fragmentShader: `
                                    uniform vec3 uVisitedColor; uniform vec3 uLandColor; uniform vec3 uWaterColor;
                                    uniform float uAlphaBoost;
                                    varying float vLandType; varying float vAlpha;
                                    void main() {
                                        float dist = length(gl_PointCoord - vec2(0.5));
                                        if (dist > 0.5) discard;
                                        float edge = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.35, 0.5, dist);
                                        vec3 col = vLandType > 1.5 ? uVisitedColor : (vLandType > 0.5 ? uLandColor : uWaterColor);
                                        gl_FragColor = vec4(col, min(vAlpha * edge * uAlphaBoost, 1.0));
                                    }`,
                                transparent: true, depthWrite: false,
                                blending: THREE.NormalBlending
                            });

                            const positions = new Float32Array(DOT_COUNT * 3);
                            const landTypeAttr = new Float32Array(DOT_COUNT);
                            const randomAttr = new Float32Array(DOT_COUNT);
                            const phi_ratio = (1 + Math.sqrt(5)) / 2;

                            for (let i = 0; i < DOT_COUNT; i++) {
                                const theta = 2 * Math.PI * i / phi_ratio;
                                const phi = Math.acos(1 - 2 * (i + 0.5) / DOT_COUNT);
                                const x = -Math.cos(theta) * Math.sin(phi) * GLOBE_RADIUS;
                                const y = Math.cos(phi) * GLOBE_RADIUS;
                                const z = Math.sin(theta) * Math.sin(phi) * GLOBE_RADIUS;
                                positions[i * 3] = x; positions[i * 3 + 1] = y; positions[i * 3 + 2] = z;
                                /* Derive lat/lon from xyz to match latLngToVec3 convention */
                                const lat = Math.asin(y / GLOBE_RADIUS) * (180 / Math.PI);
                                let lon = Math.atan2(z, -x) * (180 / Math.PI) - 180;
                                if (lon < -180) lon += 360;
                                landTypeAttr[i] = classifyPoint(lat, lon, imageData, mapW, mapH);
                                randomAttr[i] = Math.random();
                            }

                            const dotGeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
                            dotGeo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(positions, 3));
                            dotGeo.setAttribute('aLandType', new THREE.BufferAttribute(landTypeAttr, 1));
                            dotGeo.setAttribute('aRandom', new THREE.BufferAttribute(randomAttr, 1));
                            globeGroup.add(new THREE.Points(dotGeo, dotMaterial));

                            /* ── Graticule ── */
                            const graticuleMat = new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({
                                color: LAND_COLOR, transparent: true, opacity: 0.03
                            });
                            globeGroup.add(new THREE.LineSegments(
                                new THREE.WireframeGeometry(new THREE.SphereGeometry(GLOBE_RADIUS * 0.995, 36, 18)),
                                graticuleMat
                            ));

                            /* ── Country markers ── */
                            const markerGroup = new THREE.Group();
                            scene.add(markerGroup);
                            const markerMeshes = [];
                            const hitMeshes = [];

                            function latLngToVec3(lat, lng, radius) {
                                const phi = (90 - lat) * Math.PI / 180;
                                const theta = (lng + 180) * Math.PI / 180;
                                return new THREE.Vector3(
                                    -radius * Math.sin(phi) * Math.cos(theta),
                                    radius * Math.cos(phi),
                                    radius * Math.sin(phi) * Math.sin(theta)
                                );
                            }

                            const mColor = new THREE.Color(VISITED_COLOR);
                            markers.forEach((m) => {
                                const pos = latLngToVec3(m.lat, m.lng, GLOBE_RADIUS);
                                const group = new THREE.Group();
                                group.position.copy(pos);

                                const spokeGeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
                                spokeGeo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(
                                    new Float32Array([pos.x, pos.y, pos.z, 0, 0, 0]), 3
                                ));
                                markerGroup.add(new THREE.LineSegments(spokeGeo,
                                    new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({ color: mColor, transparent: true, opacity: 0.18 })
                                ));

                                group.add(new THREE.Mesh(
                                    new THREE.SphereGeometry(2.8 * MARKER_SIZE, 16, 16),
                                    new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: mColor, transparent: true, opacity: 0.04, depthWrite: false })
                                ));
                                group.add(new THREE.Mesh(
                                    new THREE.SphereGeometry(1.55 * MARKER_SIZE, 16, 16),
                                    new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: mColor, transparent: true, opacity: 0.1, depthWrite: false })
                                ));
                                const core = new THREE.Mesh(
                                    new THREE.SphereGeometry(MARKER_SIZE, 32, 32),
                                    new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
                                        color: mColor, roughness: 0.3, metalness: 0.55,
                                        emissive: mColor, emissiveIntensity: 0.12,
                                    })
                                );
                                group.add(core);

                                const hit = new THREE.Mesh(
                                    new THREE.SphereGeometry(4 * MARKER_SIZE, 8, 8),
                                    new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ transparent: true, opacity: 0, depthWrite: false })
                                );
                                hit.visible = false;
                                group.add(hit);

                                markerGroup.add(group);
                                markerMeshes.push({ group, core, data: m });
                                hitMeshes.push(hit);
                            });

                            /* ── Interaction ── */
                            const rotationQ = new THREE.Quaternion();
                            const identityQ = new THREE.Quaternion();
                            const yAxis = new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0);
                            const xAxis = new THREE.Vector3(1, 0, 0);
                            const tempQ = new THREE.Quaternion();
                            const drag = { active: false, deltaQ: new THREE.Quaternion(), lastVec: new THREE.Vector3() };
                            let elapsedTime = 0;

                            function trackballVec(x, y) {
                                const r = Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y);
                                const z = r < 0.8 ? Math.sqrt(0.8 * 0.8 - r * r) : (0.8 * 0.8) / (2 * r);
                                return new THREE.Vector3(x, y, z).normalize();
                            }

                            renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
                                drag.active = true;
                                drag.deltaQ.identity();
                                const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();
                                drag.lastVec.copy(trackballVec(
                                    ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1,
                                    -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1
                                ));
                                renderer.domElement.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
                                renderer.domElement.style.cursor = 'grabbing';
                            });
                            renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {
                                if (!drag.active) return;
                                const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();
                                const newVec = trackballVec(
                                    ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1,
                                    -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1
                                );
                                drag.deltaQ.setFromUnitVectors(drag.lastVec, newVec);
                                drag.lastVec.copy(newVec);
                            });
                            renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {
                                drag.active = false;
                                renderer.domElement.style.cursor = 'grab';
                            });
                            renderer.domElement.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => {
                                drag.active = false;
                                renderer.domElement.style.cursor = 'grab';
                            });

                            /* ── Raycaster ── */
                            const raycaster = new THREE.Raycaster();
                            const mouseNDC = new THREE.Vector2(-99, -99);
                            let hoveredIdx = null;
                            renderer.domElement.addEventListener('mousemove', e => {
                                const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();
                                mouseNDC.x = ((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1;
                                mouseNDC.y = -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1;
                            });

                            /* ── Resize ── */
                            function resize() {
                                const w = container.clientWidth;
                                const h = container.clientHeight || w;
                                renderer.setSize(w, h);
                                camera.aspect = w / h;
                                camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
                            }
                            resize();
                            window.addEventListener('resize', resize);



                            /* ── Theme ── */
                            function updateTheme() {
                                /* Globe always renders in dark style for both themes */
                            }
                            updateTheme();
                            new MutationObserver(updateTheme).observe(document.documentElement, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-theme'] });

                            /* ── Animation loop ── */
                            const clock = new THREE.Clock();
                            const euler = new THREE.Euler();

                            function animate() {
                                requestAnimationFrame(animate);
                                const dt = clock.getDelta();
                                elapsedTime += dt;

                                dotMaterial.uniforms.uTime.value = elapsedTime;
                                glowMat.uniforms.uTime.value = elapsedTime;

                                if (drag.active) {
                                    rotationQ.premultiply(drag.deltaQ);
                                } else {
                                    drag.deltaQ.slerp(identityQ, 0.08);
                                    rotationQ.premultiply(drag.deltaQ);
                                    tempQ.setFromAxisAngle(yAxis, AUTO_ROTATE_SPEED * dt);
                                    rotationQ.premultiply(tempQ);
                                    euler.setFromQuaternion(rotationQ, 'YXZ');
                                    const pitchCorrect = (0.18 * Math.sin(0.12 * elapsedTime) - euler.x) * 0.02;
                                    tempQ.setFromAxisAngle(xAxis, pitchCorrect);
                                    rotationQ.premultiply(tempQ);
                                }
                                rotationQ.normalize();
                                globeGroup.quaternion.copy(rotationQ);
                                markerGroup.quaternion.copy(rotationQ);

                                raycaster.setFromCamera(mouseNDC, camera);
                                const visible = hitMeshes.map(h => { h.visible = true; return h; });
                                const hits = raycaster.intersectObjects(visible);
                                visible.forEach(h => h.visible = false);

                                let newHovered = null;
                                if (hits.length > 0) {
                                    const idx = hitMeshes.indexOf(hits[0].object);
                                    if (idx >= 0) newHovered = idx;
                                }

                                if (newHovered !== hoveredIdx) {
                                    hoveredIdx = newHovered;
                                    if (hoveredIdx !== null) {
                                        const m = markerMeshes[hoveredIdx];
                                        const worldPos = new THREE.Vector3();
                                        m.core.getWorldPosition(worldPos);
                                        const screenPos = worldPos.clone().project(camera);
                                        const rect = renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();
                                        tooltip.textContent = m.data.name;
                                        tooltip.style.left = ((screenPos.x + 1) / 2 * rect.width) + 'px';
                                        tooltip.style.top = ((-screenPos.y + 1) / 2 * rect.height) + 'px';
                                        tooltip.style.opacity = '1';
                                    } else {
                                        tooltip.style.opacity = '0';
                                    }
                                }

                                renderer.domElement.style.cursor = hoveredIdx !== null ? 'pointer' : (drag.active ? 'grabbing' : 'grab');

                                markerMeshes.forEach((m, i) => {
                                    const target = (i === hoveredIdx) ? 1.8 : 1;
                                    const s = m.core.scale.x + (target - m.core.scale.x) * 0.15;
                                    m.core.scale.setScalar(s);
                                });

                                renderer.render(scene, camera);
                            }
                            animate();
                        })();
                        </script>


